From: portare-ch <hello@portare.org>
Subject: [PATCH] input: a game guide hotkey that shows <content>.txt in sdl3text

A text file next to the content, with the content's name and a .txt
extension, is a game guide. The new hotkey (input_game_guide) shows it
through /usr/bin/sdl3text and comes back to the game where it was.

The panel has one DRM master and the video driver holds it through its
Vulkan display instance, so the guide cannot be drawn over the game by
another process. Instead the drivers go down the way a fullscreen
toggle takes them down, sdl3text runs to completion on kmsdrm while
they are down, and they come back up. The core is not stepped in
between, so its state is untouched: no savestate, no reload.

video_driver_reinit_around() is video_driver_reinit() with a callback
between driver_uninit and drivers_init, and with the context cache
forced off, because a cached instance would keep the display.

The hotkey is exempt from the hotkey enabler, like Game Focus: it is
meant for a button no core reads (the Nova's M2), so a bare press
opens the guide and the same press in sdl3text closes it.

